[final reply]
G4 is complete and committed as `a524b54` on `feat/week6-dev-b-story-town-art`.

**What shipped (PLAN G4, story-dialogue W6-B2):**
- `scripts/world/lore_page.gd` + `scenes/dungeon/interactables/lore_page.tscn` — the walk-over pickup: `body_entered` on the interactable layer (32), host calls `StoryManager.unlock_lore(page_id)` and `queue_free()`s, a client forwards via `pickup_forwarded` in the `Chest._forward_use` shape; the profile record is written with the null-profile guard so a read without a save profile still counts for the session
- The `LORE` room populator in the same file (chest pattern): spawns the lowest-order unread page of the biome (read state = `PlayerProfile.lore_unlocked`), one page per room per SPEC-floor-generation; registration is guarded on Dev A's `FloorGenerator` (W3-A3) and notes its blocker once per process; `main.gd` registers it as the fifth line of the startup block
- JSON page validation accepting JSON's float-borne integers and parsing via `JSON.new().parse()` so malformed content warns instead of engine-erroring
- Tests: `tests/unit/test_lore_page.gd` (27 cases) + `tests/integration/test_lore_pickup.gd` (4 end-to-end cases) over 14 new fixtures, with `StoryRegistryStub` as the test double

**Verification:**
- Lore unit run 27/27 and integration 4/4 green
- Full GUT suite: **80 scripts / 1528 tests, all passing** (baseline 78/1501, the 7 stale-cache main failures resolved by `--import`)
- Headless `--smoke=3` game launch clean — the LORE blocker note appears once alongside the four existing ones, `[smoke] done, quitting`
- Two LOG.md lines appended; PLAN.md G4 left unticked and no verdict written, per instructions

READY FOR REVIEW.

